  THE RESET RULE, FOUND IN THE CORPUS AND TESTED
  Registers 1401-1410, staged in the conversation 'The Method 1.7' and never
  carried into the volumes.

  1. REGISTER 1401 -- `a` moves exactly when the running intersection of
     corridors empties.  Arithmetic on intervals alone; no subshell enters it.
     1401 prints fourteen forced moves: 37 42 43 45 55 58 64 65 80 91 96 97 103 104
     measured:                          37 42 43 45 55 58 64 65 80 91 96 97 103 104
     identical: True
     false positives (forced but not a recorded reset): none
     recorded resets NOT forced this way: Li 3, K 19, Tl 81, Fr 87

  2. THE FOUR THE RULE DOES NOT FORCE
     1401 says: 'every one the first element of a new period'.
     Li    3  first element of a period
     K    19  first element of a period
     Tl   81  NOT a period start -- it opens the 6p block, period 6 begins at Cs 55
     Fr   87  first element of a period
     3 of 4 are period openings; 1 is a block opening. 1401's wording covers three of four.

